{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570242634,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b8ca14001Xlug2ARyU3h6m9","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","messageID":"msg_1d4b8bfe5001vsS75I2r5v5uJK","type":"tool","id":"call_435950a1874849478836ea2b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"P=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements; sed -n '1,60p' $P/tasks.md; echo \"=== EVAL def ===\"; grep -n \"\\$CAP\\|\\$EVAL\\|\\$SP\\|\\$TC\" $P/tasks.md | head -20"},"output":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\"\ndescription: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that write a prompt-free health record on every hook run with a degraded flag and the newest record time, narrow the needs-a-mode label to prompts that name the hub, let the top hub name its routed command, drop the OpenCode compiled-route line, make the brief-cost script read live heads only and fix two behaviour-arm counts and one DSH session id.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"health default and brief refinements tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n| `[C]` | Coordinator task: a build, a daemon restart, a live hook run, a store under the home folder or the full suite. No worker runs it |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n- `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` and `HK` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `V <files>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <files>` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed. `VALL` is `V` with no file.\n- `MET` is `$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`. `BRF` is `$ADV/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts`. `FB` is `$HK/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`. `UPS` is `$HK/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`.\n- `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `REC` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `RCT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts`.\n- `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`. `CAP` is `$RA/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `BASE` is `$RA/command-routing-baseline.json`, `CORPUS` is `$RA/command-prompts.jsonl` and `RAR` is `$RA/README.md`. `SLICE` is `V tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\n- `S` is `$RA/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `T` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `VT` is `V tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. `OF` is `$RA/command-offer.mjs` and `VO` is `V tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`. `R` is `$RA/run-command-behaviour.mjs`.\n- `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `MBCT` is `$ADV/tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts`, a new file.\n- `PLG` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, authored in place, with `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js` a link to it. `NPLT` is `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` and `NPL` is `node --test $NPLT`, which must report `fail 0`.\n- `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n- `HD` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `HV` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`, `ARCH` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `FC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`.\n- `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, the shim every hook runtime runs.\n- `FINAL` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-final.jsonl`, read-only. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n- `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'`.\n- `EVAL` is `node $RA/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`.\n- `DRV` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check`, which must exit 0 and print `\"changed\": []`. `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0.\n\nRules for every task:\n- Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it, and no other test.\n- Re-read every file before the first edit. Phase 014 also edits `CA`, `CAP`, `R`, `S` and `DSY`. When an anchor quoted here is gone, mark the task `[B]` with the line you found and do not guess.\n- No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`. Scripts print row ids and counts only. A test or a `[C]` task may read a `tune` row's prompt from `CORPUS` by id after it checks the split.\n- No worker starts a model session, ollama, a daemon or a behaviour arm, runs `HOOK` or writes under the home folder. Only `[C]` tasks do those.\n- No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id or a rank id. State the durable reason instead. T033 checks it.\n- Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, any file under `.skilled/commands/create/`, any `package.json`, a routing input, `$ADV/lib/render.ts` or `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. Add no dependency.\n- A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n- When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n\nWorker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n- Wave 0, coordinator, one at a time: T001 (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`), T002 (`$SP/before.txt`).\n- Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before T001 confirms phase 014 is committed.\n- Wave 1, which edits no `.ts` or `.json` file under `$ADV/lib`, `$ADV/handlers`, `$ADV/schemas` or `HK`, so the build T003 captures from stays fresh: T003 (`CAP`, `BASE`), T004 (`PLG`, `NPLT`), T005 (`MBC`, `MBCT`), T006 (`S`, `T`), T007 (`DSY` and at most one test under `$DS/tests`), T008 (`HD`), T009 (`HV`), T010 (`ARCH`), T011 (`FC`).\n- Wave 2: T012 (`MET`, `STT`), T013 (`BRF`), T014 (`CA`, `CAT`, `REC`, `RCT`), T015 (`S`, `T`), T016 (`OF`), T017 (`HD`).\n- Wave 3: T018 (`FB`), T019 (`UPS`), T020 (`ST`, `SCH`, `STT`), T021 (`REC`, `RCT`), T022 (`R`).\n=== EVAL def ===\n41:- `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'`.\n56:- Wave 0, coordinator, one at a time: T001 (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`), T002 (`$SP/before.txt`).\n64:- Wave 6, coordinator, one at a time: T026 (`$SP/health-live.txt`), T027 (`$SP/live-heads.txt`), T028 (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`), T029 (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`), T030 (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`), T031 (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`).\n65:- Verification, coordinator, one at a time: T032 (`$SP/after.txt`), T033, T034 (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`).\n73:- [x] T001 [C] Confirm phase 014 is committed and list where it touched this phase's files (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`). Run `git -c core.fsmonitor=false log -1 --format='%h %s' -- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false show --name-only --format= <that commit>`, and write the files that also appear in `spec.md` section 3 into the file. Verify: the log prints one commit, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .opencode/plugins` prints nothing and the file names `CA`, `CAP`, `R`, `S` and `DSY` or says which of them phase 014 left alone.\n74:- [x] T002 [C] Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse --short HEAD`, `npm run build` in `ADV`, `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV`, `SRM`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics | [.needs_mode_floor, .needsModeRows]' $BASE` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unscored])'`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into the file. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints `[160,50,21,5]`, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `SRM` exits 0, the `BASE` line prints `[null,null]`, the summary prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,0],\"dsh\":[0,2,1],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,0]}` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 12. When a gate is red or phase 014 moved one of these values, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because every later expected value quotes these.\n83:- [x] T003 [P] Report the rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)` and recapture the baseline (`CAP`, `BASE`). Add `const PROMPT_POLICY_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/prompt-policy.js')` beside `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE`, add it to the array the existence loop checks, import `extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions` from it after the `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE` import and add `routeNeedsMode` to that import's names. Before the corpus loop, declare `needsModeRows` as an empty array and `needsModeFloor` as 0. Inside the loop, hold the hub's route as `const route = topId !== undefined && COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS.has(topId) ? readCompiledRoute(workspaceRoot, topId, row.prompt) : undefined` and pass `route` to `attachCommand` where the call reads the route inline today, so the label reuses the same lookup. After the line that sets `delivered`, add `const needsMode = route !== undefined && delivered === undefined && routeNeedsMode(topId, route, extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions(row.prompt))` and push `row.id` into `needsModeRows` when it is true. Inside the `wantsSilence` block, add 1 to `needsModeFloor` when `needsMode` is true. In `attachedMetrics`, right after `attachedRows`, add `needs_mode_floor: { count: needsModeFloor, total: falseOfferTotal }` and `needsModeRows: needsModeRows.sort()`. Above the `needsMode` line, add a comment saying a head shows that label only when nothing else names a command, so a row counts only when neither the typed command nor the route delivered one, and a silent row that carries it shows a label nobody asked for. Then run `node $CAP --write`. The build still holds the old rule, which ignores the third argument, so this capture records the before rows. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":3,\"total\":35}`, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows | length' $BASE` prints 16, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[]' $BASE | rg -c '^(nm-sk-design-01|nm-sk-doc-01|nm-system-skill-advisor-01|cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01|cmd-create-repo-rule-plain-tune-01)$'` prints 5, `diff <(jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha, .attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows)' $BASE) <(git -c core.fsmonitor=false show HEAD:$BASE | jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha)')` prints nothing and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n112:- [x] T035 Publish no holdout id in the needs-a-mode row list (`CAP`, `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`). Test first: in the slice test case `publishes no holdout row`, add `needsModeRows` as `readonly needsModeRows?: readonly string[]` to the `attached` type and add `...(attached.needsModeRows ?? [])` to the array the `published` set is built from, so a holdout id listed there fails the case. Run `SLICE` and see that case fail naming 8 holdout ids. Then in `CAP`, change `if (needsMode) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` to `if (needsMode && publishRow) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` and add a comment above it saying the list names rows with their outcome, so a holdout row stays out of it as it stays out of the row maps. Do not run `node $CAP --write`, a later task recaptures. Read only `id` and `split` from the corpus and print no holdout prompt. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0 and `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[] | select(test(\"holdout\"))] | length'` prints 0, and `rg -c \"needsMode && publishRow\" $CAP` prints 1.\n119:- [x] T024 [P] Recapture the baseline on the rebuilt label rule (`BASE`). Run `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":1,\"total\":35}` and `[\"nm-system-skill-advisor-01\"]`, the T003 `diff` against `HEAD` prints nothing, `FLOOR` prints the four lines `$SP/before.txt` holds for it and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n123:- [x] T026 [C] Prove the default record on a real hook run (`$SP/health-live.txt`). Take `D` from `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/metrics.js').then((m) => console.log(m.advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())))\"` and record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, 0 when the file is absent. Pipe `{\"prompt\":\"write a README for the utils folder\",\"cwd\":\"<worktree root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"health-check\"}` into `env -u SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG node $HOOK`, then record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, `tail -1 \"$D\" | jq -c '[has(\"skillLabel\"), has(\"errorDetails\"), .runtime, .status, .timestamp]'` and `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.js').then((m) => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot: process.cwd() }).hookHealth)))\"`. Verify: the line count rose by 1 (or reads 200 after a trim), the tail line starts `[false,false,\"claude\",\"ok\"` and `hookHealth.lastRecordAt` equals the tail line's `timestamp`.\n124:- [x] T027 [C] Read four live heads on the rebuilt daemon (`$SP/live-heads.txt`). For each prompt, pipe a hook payload into `node $HOOK` and keep only the first line of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`: the prompts of `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01`, each read from `CORPUS` by id with `jq` after checking that its split is `tune`, then `use the sk-doc skill` and `use the system-deep-loop skill`. Write each head beside its label, never the corpus prompt. Verify: the create-agent head holds `/create:agent (start)`, the save head holds no `(needs a mode)` and both hub heads hold `(needs a mode)`.\n125:- [x] T028 [C] Rerun the OpenCode render probe (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`). Run `node specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/render-entries.mjs > $SP/render-entries-after.json`. Verify: `jq -r '.rows[] | [.label, (.pluginEntries|length)] | @tsv' $SP/render-entries-after.json` prints 1 on all nine labels.\n126:- [x] T029 [C] Prove the DSH session choice on the stored final arm (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`). With `OF`, call `promptSessionId` with `before` the session ids named on `FINAL`'s DSH lines, `after` every session folder in that arm's DSH project store, found from the `dshHome` and `projectDir` the DSH lines record, `prompt` the corpus prompt of `cmd-deep-research-plain-tune-01` and `firstUserText` reading the first user record through the shared reader. Print only the chosen id and the candidate ids with their record counts. Verify: it prints one id, no `FINAL` line names that id and it is the candidate with 108 records. When the store is gone, mark the task `[B]` and change no code.\n127:- [x] T030 [C] Run the brief-cost script once (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost-live.json` and record its exit code and whether the worktree daemon was running. Verify: either exit 0 with `liveRows` above 0 and a `medianHeadBytes`, or exit 2 with `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}`. Record which, and change no code on either answer.\n128:- [x] T031 [C] Score the final arm with the new counts (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`). Run `node $S --summary $FINAL --json > $SP/summary-final-after.json` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -c 'map_values([.post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])'`. Verify: `jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])' $SP/summary-final-after.json` prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,1],\"dsh\":[1,2,2],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,1]}` and the second command prints claude `[0,0]`, devin `[2,1]`, dsh `[2,2]`, opencode `[2,0]` and pi `[1,1]`. A differing value is reported, never matched by changing code.\n136:- [x] T032 [C] Run every floor (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV` and `SRM` and write each output beside its line in `$SP/before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints the four lines `before.txt` holds, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its `before.txt` line with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []` and `SRM` exits 0.\n148:- [x] `BASE` reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35, `$SP/summary-final-after.json` prints the SC-002 line and every floor holds against `$SP/before.txt`\n183:- [x] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 014 is committed and its shared files are listed before wave 1 (T001). Evidence: `$SP/phase-014-files.txt`. Done 2026-11-13: the file names commit `b3b5ae8314`, lists `command-attach.ts`, the capture, the runner, the scorer and `doctor-setup.yaml` among its files and reads `(end of status)` for the status.\n192:- [x] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on `CAP`, `MBC`, `S`, `OF`, `R` and `PLG`. Evidence: `TC` in `$SP/after.txt` and the six `node --check` exits. Done 2026-11-13: `TC` exits 0 in `scratch/after.txt` and again at close-out, and `node --check` exits 0 on all six files.\n203:- [x] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T032). Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt`. Done 2026-11-13: every `scratch/after.txt` floor equals its `before.txt` line. The `VALL` rerun after T039 reads 1755 passed and 0 failed.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\"\ndescription: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that write a prompt-free health record on every hook run with a degraded flag and the newest record time, narrow the needs-a-mode label to prompts that name the hub, let the top hub name its routed command, drop the OpenCode compiled-route line, make the brief-cost script read live heads only and fix two behaviour-arm counts and one DSH session id.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"health default and brief refinements tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n| `[C]` | Coordinator task: a build, a daemon restart, a live hook run, a store under the home folder or the full suite. No worker runs it |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n- `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` and `HK` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `V <files>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <files>` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed. `VALL` is `V` with no file.\n- `MET` is `$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`. `BRF` is `$ADV/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts`. `FB` is `$HK/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`. `UPS` is `$HK/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`.\n- `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `REC` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `RCT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts`.\n- `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`. `CAP` is `$RA/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `BASE` is `$RA/command-routing-baseline.json`, `CORPUS` is `$RA/command-prompts.jsonl` and `RAR` is `$RA/README.md`. `SLICE` is `V tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\n- `S` is `$RA/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `T` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `VT` is `V tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. `OF` is `$RA/command-offer.mjs` and `VO` is `V tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`. `R` is `$RA/run-command-behaviour.mjs`.\n- `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `MBCT` is `$ADV/tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts`, a new file.\n- `PLG` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, authored in place, with `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js` a link to it. `NPLT` is `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` and `NPL` is `node --test $NPLT`, which must report `fail 0`.\n- `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n- `HD` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `HV` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`, `ARCH` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `FC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`.\n- `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, the shim every hook runtime runs.\n- `FINAL` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-final.jsonl`, read-only. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n- `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'`.\n- `EVAL` is `node $RA/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`.\n- `DRV` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check`, which must exit 0 and print `\"changed\": []`. `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0.\n\nRules for every task:\n- Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it, and no other test.\n- Re-read every file before the first edit. Phase 014 also edits `CA`, `CAP`, `R`, `S` and `DSY`. When an anchor quoted here is gone, mark the task `[B]` with the line you found and do not guess.\n- No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`. Scripts print row ids and counts only. A test or a `[C]` task may read a `tune` row's prompt from `CORPUS` by id after it checks the split.\n- No worker starts a model session, ollama, a daemon or a behaviour arm, runs `HOOK` or writes under the home folder. Only `[C]` tasks do those.\n- No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id or a rank id. State the durable reason instead. T033 checks it.\n- Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, any file under `.skilled/commands/create/`, any `package.json`, a routing input, `$ADV/lib/render.ts` or `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. Add no dependency.\n- A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n- When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n\nWorker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n- Wave 0, coordinator, one at a time: T001 (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`), T002 (`$SP/before.txt`).\n- Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before T001 confirms phase 014 is committed.\n- Wave 1, which edits no `.ts` or `.json` file under `$ADV/lib`, `$ADV/handlers`, `$ADV/schemas` or `HK`, so the build T003 captures from stays fresh: T003 (`CAP`, `BASE`), T004 (`PLG`, `NPLT`), T005 (`MBC`, `MBCT`), T006 (`S`, `T`), T007 (`DSY` and at most one test under `$DS/tests`), T008 (`HD`), T009 (`HV`), T010 (`ARCH`), T011 (`FC`).\n- Wave 2: T012 (`MET`, `STT`), T013 (`BRF`), T014 (`CA`, `CAT`, `REC`, `RCT`), T015 (`S`, `T`), T016 (`OF`), T017 (`HD`).\n- Wave 3: T018 (`FB`), T019 (`UPS`), T020 (`ST`, `SCH`, `STT`), T021 (`REC`, `RCT`), T022 (`R`).\n=== EVAL def ===\n41:- `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'`.\n56:- Wave 0, coordinator, one at a time: T001 (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`), T002 (`$SP/before.txt`).\n64:- Wave 6, coordinator, one at a time: T026 (`$SP/health-live.txt`), T027 (`$SP/live-heads.txt`), T028 (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`), T029 (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`), T030 (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`), T031 (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`).\n65:- Verification, coordinator, one at a time: T032 (`$SP/after.txt`), T033, T034 (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`).\n73:- [x] T001 [C] Confirm phase 014 is committed and list where it touched this phase's files (`$SP/phase-014-files.txt`). Run `git -c core.fsmonitor=false log -1 --format='%h %s' -- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false show --name-only --format= <that commit>`, and write the files that also appear in `spec.md` section 3 into the file. Verify: the log prints one commit, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .opencode/plugins` prints nothing and the file names `CA`, `CAP`, `R`, `S` and `DSY` or says which of them phase 014 left alone.\n74:- [x] T002 [C] Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse --short HEAD`, `npm run build` in `ADV`, `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV`, `SRM`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics | [.needs_mode_floor, .needsModeRows]' $BASE` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unscored])'`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into the file. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints `[160,50,21,5]`, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `SRM` exits 0, the `BASE` line prints `[null,null]`, the summary prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,0],\"dsh\":[0,2,1],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,0]}` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 12. When a gate is red or phase 014 moved one of these values, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because every later expected value quotes these.\n83:- [x] T003 [P] Report the rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)` and recapture the baseline (`CAP`, `BASE`). Add `const PROMPT_POLICY_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/prompt-policy.js')` beside `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE`, add it to the array the existence loop checks, import `extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions` from it after the `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE` import and add `routeNeedsMode` to that import's names. Before the corpus loop, declare `needsModeRows` as an empty array and `needsModeFloor` as 0. Inside the loop, hold the hub's route as `const route = topId !== undefined && COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS.has(topId) ? readCompiledRoute(workspaceRoot, topId, row.prompt) : undefined` and pass `route` to `attachCommand` where the call reads the route inline today, so the label reuses the same lookup. After the line that sets `delivered`, add `const needsMode = route !== undefined && delivered === undefined && routeNeedsMode(topId, route, extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions(row.prompt))` and push `row.id` into `needsModeRows` when it is true. Inside the `wantsSilence` block, add 1 to `needsModeFloor` when `needsMode` is true. In `attachedMetrics`, right after `attachedRows`, add `needs_mode_floor: { count: needsModeFloor, total: falseOfferTotal }` and `needsModeRows: needsModeRows.sort()`. Above the `needsMode` line, add a comment saying a head shows that label only when nothing else names a command, so a row counts only when neither the typed command nor the route delivered one, and a silent row that carries it shows a label nobody asked for. Then run `node $CAP --write`. The build still holds the old rule, which ignores the third argument, so this capture records the before rows. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":3,\"total\":35}`, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows | length' $BASE` prints 16, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[]' $BASE | rg -c '^(nm-sk-design-01|nm-sk-doc-01|nm-system-skill-advisor-01|cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01|cmd-create-repo-rule-plain-tune-01)$'` prints 5, `diff <(jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha, .attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows)' $BASE) <(git -c core.fsmonitor=false show HEAD:$BASE | jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha)')` prints nothing and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n112:- [x] T035 Publish no holdout id in the needs-a-mode row list (`CAP`, `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`). Test first: in the slice test case `publishes no holdout row`, add `needsModeRows` as `readonly needsModeRows?: readonly string[]` to the `attached` type and add `...(attached.needsModeRows ?? [])` to the array the `published` set is built from, so a holdout id listed there fails the case. Run `SLICE` and see that case fail naming 8 holdout ids. Then in `CAP`, change `if (needsMode) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` to `if (needsMode && publishRow) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` and add a comment above it saying the list names rows with their outcome, so a holdout row stays out of it as it stays out of the row maps. Do not run `node $CAP --write`, a later task recaptures. Read only `id` and `split` from the corpus and print no holdout prompt. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0 and `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[] | select(test(\"holdout\"))] | length'` prints 0, and `rg -c \"needsMode && publishRow\" $CAP` prints 1.\n119:- [x] T024 [P] Recapture the baseline on the rebuilt label rule (`BASE`). Run `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":1,\"total\":35}` and `[\"nm-system-skill-advisor-01\"]`, the T003 `diff` against `HEAD` prints nothing, `FLOOR` prints the four lines `$SP/before.txt` holds for it and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n123:- [x] T026 [C] Prove the default record on a real hook run (`$SP/health-live.txt`). Take `D` from `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/metrics.js').then((m) => console.log(m.advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())))\"` and record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, 0 when the file is absent. Pipe `{\"prompt\":\"write a README for the utils folder\",\"cwd\":\"<worktree root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"health-check\"}` into `env -u SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG node $HOOK`, then record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, `tail -1 \"$D\" | jq -c '[has(\"skillLabel\"), has(\"errorDetails\"), .runtime, .status, .timestamp]'` and `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.js').then((m) => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot: process.cwd() }).hookHealth)))\"`. Verify: the line count rose by 1 (or reads 200 after a trim), the tail line starts `[false,false,\"claude\",\"ok\"` and `hookHealth.lastRecordAt` equals the tail line's `timestamp`.\n124:- [x] T027 [C] Read four live heads on the rebuilt daemon (`$SP/live-heads.txt`). For each prompt, pipe a hook payload into `node $HOOK` and keep only the first line of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`: the prompts of `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01`, each read from `CORPUS` by id with `jq` after checking that its split is `tune`, then `use the sk-doc skill` and `use the system-deep-loop skill`. Write each head beside its label, never the corpus prompt. Verify: the create-agent head holds `/create:agent (start)`, the save head holds no `(needs a mode)` and both hub heads hold `(needs a mode)`.\n125:- [x] T028 [C] Rerun the OpenCode render probe (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`). Run `node specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/render-entries.mjs > $SP/render-entries-after.json`. Verify: `jq -r '.rows[] | [.label, (.pluginEntries|length)] | @tsv' $SP/render-entries-after.json` prints 1 on all nine labels.\n126:- [x] T029 [C] Prove the DSH session choice on the stored final arm (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`). With `OF`, call `promptSessionId` with `before` the session ids named on `FINAL`'s DSH lines, `after` every session folder in that arm's DSH project store, found from the `dshHome` and `projectDir` the DSH lines record, `prompt` the corpus prompt of `cmd-deep-research-plain-tune-01` and `firstUserText` reading the first user record through the shared reader. Print only the chosen id and the candidate ids with their record counts. Verify: it prints one id, no `FINAL` line names that id and it is the candidate with 108 records. When the store is gone, mark the task `[B]` and change no code.\n127:- [x] T030 [C] Run the brief-cost script once (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost-live.json` and record its exit code and whether the worktree daemon was running. Verify: either exit 0 with `liveRows` above 0 and a `medianHeadBytes`, or exit 2 with `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}`. Record which, and change no code on either answer.\n128:- [x] T031 [C] Score the final arm with the new counts (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`). Run `node $S --summary $FINAL --json > $SP/summary-final-after.json` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -c 'map_values([.post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])'`. Verify: `jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])' $SP/summary-final-after.json` prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,1],\"dsh\":[1,2,2],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,1]}` and the second command prints claude `[0,0]`, devin `[2,1]`, dsh `[2,2]`, opencode `[2,0]` and pi `[1,1]`. A differing value is reported, never matched by changing code.\n136:- [x] T032 [C] Run every floor (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV` and `SRM` and write each output beside its line in `$SP/before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints the four lines `before.txt` holds, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its `before.txt` line with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []` and `SRM` exits 0.\n148:- [x] `BASE` reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35, `$SP/summary-final-after.json` prints the SC-002 line and every floor holds against `$SP/before.txt`\n183:- [x] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 014 is committed and its shared files are listed before wave 1 (T001). Evidence: `$SP/phase-014-files.txt`. Done 2026-11-13: the file names commit `b3b5ae8314`, lists `command-attach.ts`, the capture, the runner, the scorer and `doctor-setup.yaml` among its files and reads `(end of status)` for the status.\n192:- [x] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on `CAP`, `MBC`, `S`, `OF`, `R` and `PLG`. Evidence: `TC` in `$SP/after.txt` and the six `node --check` exits. Done 2026-11-13: `TC` exits 0 in `scratch/after.txt` and again at close-out, and `node --check` exits 0 on all six files.\n203:- [x] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T032). Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt`. Done 2026-11-13: every `scratch/after.txt` floor equals its `before.txt` line. The `VALL` rerun after T039 reads 1755 passed and 0 failed.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"P=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements; sed -n '1,60p' $P/tasks.md; echo \\\"=== EVAL def ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"\\\\$CAP\\\\|\\\\$EVAL\\\\|\\\\$SP\\\\|\\\\$TC\\\" $P/tasks.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570242580,"end":1794570242634}}}}
