{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570377312,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4baada3001uNLHoKy2ElrEyG","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","messageID":"msg_1d4ba922d001Otb1YArjPN9UX8","type":"tool","id":"call_303baeb485364cd797b9b2a2","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/deep-research-strategy.md","content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - inprocess-timing-4\ndescription: Timing lane for segment three rank 6, the in-process TypeScript handler on the degraded advisor path.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"in-process advisor timing\"\n  - \"degraded path timing\"\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - inprocess-timing-4\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nMeasure the cold and warm cost of scoring a degraded prompt with the TypeScript handler in process, as segment three rank 6 proposes, against the hook's 2.5 s budget and today's Python fallback scorer, then answer build or decline.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Init fills Topic, Key Questions, Known Context and Research Boundaries.\n- Each iteration writes its evidence to `iterations/iteration-NNN.md`.\n- The reducer refreshes the machine-owned sections after every iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nLANE inprocess-timing-4 (segment three rank 6). Phases 014 and 015 are built. Rank 6 proposes that `runLocalScorer` call `handleAdvisorRecommend` in process and then apply the Q026 filter (`degradedRecommendations`). Measure cold and warm cost, compare with today's Python fallback scorer on the same prompts, check the 2.5 s hook budget and the floors, and answer build or decline with numbers.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] What does one in-process handler call cost from a cold node process, and does its worst case fit the hook's 2.5 s budget?\n- [ ] What does a warm handler call cost in a process that already loaded the modules, and how much of the cold cost is module load rather than scoring?\n- [ ] How does the in-process handler compare with today's Python fallback scorer on the same prompts?\n- [ ] Would the in-process answer change the degraded top, the typed command and the mode label under the Q026 filter, and do the floors hold?\n- [ ] How much of the hook's 2.5 s budget is left when the degraded CLI path uses the in-process handler instead of the Python spawn?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Do not change tracked code, the tracked database, or any file outside the lineage folder.\n- Do not start a model session, a behaviour arm, a daemon, or an Ollama pull; use the embedder already running.\n- Do not read or print holdout prompt text; counts only, through the committed scripts.\n- Do not reopen ranks already built, declined or waiting in segments one to three.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Stop when the five key questions above are answered with commands and quoted output.\n- Stop when a further iteration would add no new measurement.\n- Never exceed config.maxIterations.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. The handler is `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, compiled at `ADV/dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.js`.\n- Today's local scorer is `ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts` `runLocalScorer` at lines 1455-1475, which spawns `python3 ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py` through `runAdvisorSubprocess` (`ADV/lib/subprocess.ts:305-409`).\n- The Q026 filter is `degradedRecommendations` at `ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1481-1526`.\n- The hook's budget is `DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500` at `hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:144`, and the hook's own advisor options are at `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:228-247`.\n- The DB path override is `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` at `ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:303-320`, so a scratch copy leaves the tracked database untouched.\n- Floors: `node $RA/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'` with `RA=ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Question injection surface: not used in this lineage\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-13T11:45:49Z\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/deep-research-strategy.md\",\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - inprocess-timing-4\\ndescription: Timing lane for segment three rank 6, the in-process TypeScript handler on the degraded advisor path.\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"in-process advisor timing\\\"\\n  - \\\"degraded path timing\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - inprocess-timing-4\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nMeasure the cold and warm cost of scoring a degraded prompt with the TypeScript handler in process, as segment three rank 6 proposes, against the hook's 2.5 s budget and today's Python fallback scorer, then answer build or decline.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Init fills Topic, Key Questions, Known Context and Research Boundaries.\\n- Each iteration writes its evidence to `iterations/iteration-NNN.md`.\\n- The reducer refreshes the machine-owned sections after every iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nLANE inprocess-timing-4 (segment three rank 6). Phases 014 and 015 are built. Rank 6 proposes that `runLocalScorer` call `handleAdvisorRecommend` in process and then apply the Q026 filter (`degradedRecommendations`). Measure cold and warm cost, compare with today's Python fallback scorer on the same prompts, check the 2.5 s hook budget and the floors, and answer build or decline with numbers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] What does one in-process handler call cost from a cold node process, and does its worst case fit the hook's 2.5 s budget?\\n- [ ] What does a warm handler call cost in a process that already loaded the modules, and how much of the cold cost is module load rather than scoring?\\n- [ ] How does the in-process handler compare with today's Python fallback scorer on the same prompts?\\n- [ ] Would the in-process answer change the degraded top, the typed command and the mode label under the Q026 filter, and do the floors hold?\\n- [ ] How much of the hook's 2.5 s budget is left when the degraded CLI path uses the in-process handler instead of the Python spawn?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Do not change tracked code, the tracked database, or any file outside the lineage folder.\\n- Do not start a model session, a behaviour arm, a daemon, or an Ollama pull; use the embedder already running.\\n- Do not read or print holdout prompt text; counts only, through the committed scripts.\\n- Do not reopen ranks already built, declined or waiting in segments one to three.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Stop when the five key questions above are answered with commands and quoted output.\\n- Stop when a further iteration would add no new measurement.\\n- Never exceed config.maxIterations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. The handler is `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, compiled at `ADV/dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.js`.\\n- Today's local scorer is `ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts` `runLocalScorer` at lines 1455-1475, which spawns `python3 ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py` through `runAdvisorSubprocess` (`ADV/lib/subprocess.ts:305-409`).\\n- The Q026 filter is `degradedRecommendations` at `ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1481-1526`.\\n- The hook's budget is `DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500` at `hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:144`, and the hook's own advisor options are at `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:228-247`.\\n- The DB path override is `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` at `ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:303-320`, so a scratch copy leaves the tracked database untouched.\\n- Floors: `node $RA/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'` with `RA=ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Question injection surface: not used in this lineage\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-13T11:45:49Z\\n\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570366371,"end":1794570377312}}}}
