{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570732576,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c0298d00282RVJfRzYZDR9F","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","messageID":"msg_1d4bff71c001oKAvYousXAZHRr","type":"tool","id":"call_d126caa0b88a4564a27546b9","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Command Surfacing Research: In-Process Handler Timing (inprocess-timing-4)\n\nLineage of segment four. Lane: segment three rank 6, the in-process TypeScript handler on the degraded advisor path. Every number comes from a command run inside this lineage; every scratch artifact is under `scratch/`.\n\n## 1. Question\n\nRank 6 proposes that `runLocalScorer` call `handleAdvisorRecommend` in process with the hook's options, then apply the Q026 filter (`degradedRecommendations`). Does that fit the hook's 2.5 s budget from a cold process, how does it compare with today's Python fallback scorer, and does it change the degraded answer?\n\n## 2. Method\n\n- The tracked database and generation file were copied to `scratch/db/` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` pointed at the copy. No tracked file is written.\n- `scratch/timing-handler.mjs` imports the built handler `dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.js` with the hook's options and scores ten fixed non-holdout prompts.\n- Cold: ten fresh `node` processes, one prompt each. Warm: one process, ten distinct prompts after two warm-up rows outside the measured set. Fallback: `runAdvisorSubprocess`, the Python scorer `runLocalScorer` spawns today, one spawn per prompt.\n- Floors: the committed capture `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`.\n\n## 3. Findings So Far\n\n### Iteration 1\n\n- Cold import plus one handler call: median 224.7 ms, worst 337.7 ms. Whole fresh process: median 239.4 ms, worst 443.0 ms, 17.7 percent of the 2,500 ms budget.\n- Warm handler call: median 76.5 ms, worst 93.6 ms.\n- Handler import: median 78.4 ms, 35 percent of the cold added median.\n- Today's Python fallback spawn: median 238.5 ms, worst 377.7 ms on the same prompts.\n- Cold added cost is at parity with the fallback (minus 13.8 ms); the warm call is 3.1 times cheaper.\n- Floors unchanged: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, plain tune 23 of 45, attached false offers 0 of 35.\n\n## 4. Open Questions\n\n- Does the in-process answer change the degraded top, the typed command and the mode label under the Q026 filter?\n- How much of the 2.5 s hook budget is left when the degraded CLI uses the in-process handler instead of the Python spawn?\n- Build or decline, with the numbers.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/research.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/research.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/research.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Command Surfacing Research: In-Process Handler Timing (inprocess-timing-4)\\n\\nLineage of segment four. Lane: segment three rank 6, the in-process TypeScript handler on the degraded advisor path. Every number comes from a command run inside this lineage; every scratch artifact is under `scratch/`.\\n\\n## 1. Question\\n\\nRank 6 proposes that `runLocalScorer` call `handleAdvisorRecommend` in process with the hook's options, then apply the Q026 filter (`degradedRecommendations`). Does that fit the hook's 2.5 s budget from a cold process, how does it compare with today's Python fallback scorer, and does it change the degraded answer?\\n\\n## 2. Method\\n\\n- The tracked database and generation file were copied to `scratch/db/` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` pointed at the copy. No tracked file is written.\\n- `scratch/timing-handler.mjs` imports the built handler `dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.js` with the hook's options and scores ten fixed non-holdout prompts.\\n- Cold: ten fresh `node` processes, one prompt each. Warm: one process, ten distinct prompts after two warm-up rows outside the measured set. Fallback: `runAdvisorSubprocess`, the Python scorer `runLocalScorer` spawns today, one spawn per prompt.\\n- Floors: the committed capture `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`.\\n\\n## 3. Findings So Far\\n\\n### Iteration 1\\n\\n- Cold import plus one handler call: median 224.7 ms, worst 337.7 ms. Whole fresh process: median 239.4 ms, worst 443.0 ms, 17.7 percent of the 2,500 ms budget.\\n- Warm handler call: median 76.5 ms, worst 93.6 ms.\\n- Handler import: median 78.4 ms, 35 percent of the cold added median.\\n- Today's Python fallback spawn: median 238.5 ms, worst 377.7 ms on the same prompts.\\n- Cold added cost is at parity with the fallback (minus 13.8 ms); the warm call is 3.1 times cheaper.\\n- Floors unchanged: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, plain tune 23 of 45, attached false offers 0 of 35.\\n\\n## 4. Open Questions\\n\\n- Does the in-process answer change the degraded top, the typed command and the mode label under the Q026 filter?\\n- How much of the 2.5 s hook budget is left when the degraded CLI uses the in-process handler instead of the Python spawn?\\n- Build or decline, with the numbers.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570725773,"end":1794570732576}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570735516,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c03f000016yjLzyMN1WbhfD","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abdd3ffe0ORlG2coZj9Q9y","messageID":"msg_1d4bff71c001oKAvYousXAZHRr","type":"tool","id":"call_81ce3aefacd64367836c0092","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"L=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/inprocess-timing-4\nexport SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR=\"$PWD/$L/scratch/db\"\nexport SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1\ndate -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\nnode \"$L/scratch/timing-handler.mjs\" shape > \"$L/scratch/shape.jsonl\" 2> \"$L/scratch/shape.err\"; echo \"SHAPE_EXIT=$?\"; cat \"$L/scratch/shape.jsonl\"; echo \"--- err ---\"; cat \"$L/scratch/shape.err\"","timeout":240000},"output":"2026-11-13T11:52:12Z\nSHAPE_EXIT=0\n{\"mode\":\"shape\",\"index\":0,\"id\":\"cmd-create-readme-plain-tune-01\",\"split\":\"tune\",\"inProcessMs\":131.953,\"fallbackMs\":190.971,\"inProcess\":{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":null,\"kind\":null,\"count\":2,\"commandKept\":false},\"fallback\":{\"top\":\"system-spec-kit\",\"command\":null,\"kind\":null,\"count\":1,\"commandKept\":false},\"rawHandlerTop\":{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":null,\"needsMode\":false,\"kind\":\"skill\"}}\n{\"mode\":\"shape\",\"index\":1,\"id\":\"cmd-doctor-setup-plain-tune-01\",\"split\":\"tune\",\"inProcessMs\":68.94854199999997,\"fallbackMs\":169.748667,\"inProcess\":{\"top\":null,\"command\":null,\"kind\":null,\"count\":0,\"commandKept\":false},\"fallback\":{\"top\":\"sk-code\",\"command\":null,\"kind\":null,\"count\":1,\"commandKept\":false},\"rawHandlerTop\":{\"top\":null,\"command\":null,\"needsMode\":false,\"kind\":null}}\n{\"mode\":\"shape\",\"index\":2,\"id\":\"cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01\",\"split\":\"tune\",\"inProcessMs\":78.38070800000003,\"fallbackMs\":163.905125,\"inProcess\":{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":null,\"kind\":nu